All 5 tests pass.

**Bug:** In `/workspace/median.py`, the function always returned the upper-middle element (`s[n // 2]`), which is only correct for odd-length lists. For even-length lists, the median is the average of the two middle values.

**Fix:** Branch on parity — return `s[mid]` when odd, otherwise `(s[mid - 1] + s[mid]) / 2`. Test file untouched.

